<title>ITALY: Bank of Italy sets 10.5 trillion lire repo tender.</title>
<headline>Bank of Italy sets 10.5 trillion lire repo tender.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Italy said it called a 10.5 trillion lire repurchase tender for today for government securities to be resold on January 2.</p>
<p>At the previous comparable 10-day operation for 9.0 trillion lire on December 23, the minimum accepted rate stood at 7.67 percent and the average rate at 7.76 percent.</p>
</text>
